window.docContents[216].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--Errors-prevented":{"contents":"* Summing what does not sum: the normal-mode frequency taken as the sum of the bodies' angular frequencies. assemble fails because no Assembles instance exists (HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_frequency_assembly).* Wrong composition law: the stiffnesses of springs in series added as if the springs were in parallel (HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_series_stiffness).* Whole/part confusion: pair P's mass added to body A's mass, a quantity about the whole combined with a quantity about one of its parts (HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_whole_part).\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L2 — The pair is a system too\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.3.1.4. Errors prevented","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--Errors-prevented"}});